{
  "provenance": "Synthetic stand-in input, not captured: no authenticated `gh` (and no winget, soffice.com) is available on the recording machine. Node and the core are both run against these same rules and compared with each other, so the rules are input, never expected values. Each rule's `imitates` names the command and the documented output shape it stands for, so a wrong imitation can be found later. A rule with `effect` also runs those git commands in the child's directory so the repository changes as with the real tool.",
  "note": "The scripted GitHub CLI (and its package managers) of the phone-scm recording: every process the Node host spawned for `gh`, `winget`, `soffice.com` and `git --version` is answered from these rules, never run. A rule matches argv token by token ('*' any one token, '**' the rest); the first rule whose `when` holds in the world and whose argv matches answers, then `set` changes the world. An argv no rule matches fails the recording. The Rust side scripts its gh runner with the same rules.",
  "world": {
    "ghInstalled": false,
    "ghAuth": false,
    "wingetMissing": false,
    "wingetFails": false,
    "wingetInstallsGh": true,
    "gitMissing": false,
    "wingetInstallsGit": true,
    "soffice": false,
    "wingetInstallsSoffice": true,
    "starred": false,
    "ghApiDown": false
  },
  "gitPath": "C:\\Program Files\\Git\\mingw64\\bin\\git.exe",
